    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "# Technopoly — Neil Postman",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "4d9c9e0ae9a64a2b842a5eddeb7005d3",
    "entityId": "51866b23206240a4bd7157abed5636dd",
    "typeId": "beaba5cba67741a8b35377030613fc70",
    "toEntityId": "087a37e26c7c4f4e9a900eb7888821ce",
    "toEntity": {
      "name": null
    },
    "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72",
    "position": "a1A7U",
    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "The book argues against mindlessly implementing technology — treating it as a neutral or inevitable force rather than asking what it costs us. I think this is incredibly true in education.",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "bf2c64ac36074b3aa68a160df1030647",
    "entityId": "efed1a66ca4940eaa71e4035f865dbc1",
    "typeId": "beaba5cba67741a8b35377030613fc70",
    "toEntityId": "845156f31d774954b9ad987075f5c854",
    "toEntity": {
      "name": null
    },
    "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72",
    "position": "a22jr",
    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "There's a whole section on statistics and how grades and organizational rankings have reshaped how we think about accomplishment and knowledge. As a teacher, it was obvious to me that a student's grade was not the same as their actual understanding — but so much time and effort went into putting a number on students that it materially took away from my ability to build relationships and learn with them in a more human way.",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "982a69cfddff471c86bc08d7869df029",
    "entityId": "e60a5ebd447f4d33a9db4738dc63678c",
    "typeId": "beaba5cba67741a8b35377030613fc70",
    "toEntityId": "a11ae1c60e1d4bfcb8286092d8ea6e8d",
    "toEntity": {
      "name": null
    },
    "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72",
    "position": "a384F",
    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "It could go both ways: a student who scored high might carry a deeper misconception, while a student who struggled on an exam could have a rich appreciation for logical thinking — their difficulty performing under assessment conditions masking genuine understanding.",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "195cbe61fa7844318983e72b8ecb3a6b",
    "entityId": "a97422605d3149efb67e0f184ab3b239",
    "typeId": "beaba5cba67741a8b35377030613fc70",
    "toEntityId": "b312dbbd3dea4aa7854e0105cc81cffc",
    "toEntity": {
      "name": null
    },
    "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72",
    "position": "a438I",
    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "Real understanding showed up in human interaction — reading a paper carefully, noticing stray marks on diagrams, the exact wording chosen in a written answer, or a live discussion in the hallway. I found very little value in the insight supposedly granted by constant testing; whatever value existed was overshadowed by the cost in time and effort for both me and the students.",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "d639694fb2434727ab91fe5d84a85f38",
    "entityId": "e180c868dbab4cc799c7b6e48f261e02",
    "typeId": "beaba5cba67741a8b35377030613fc70",
    "toEntityId": "bdc56e126bb84895b6bdd1ecbc670020",
    "toEntity": {
      "name": null
    },
    "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72",
    "position": "a58MM",
    "content": {
      "values": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "propertyId": "e3e363d1dd294ccb8e6ff3b76d99bc33",
            "text": "That reclaimed time could go toward shared experiences, larger and messier problems rooted in real life, helping students grapple with human and social questions. Using tools — mathematics included — to accomplish real goals with thoughtfulness, rather than mindlessly applying algorithms to rote problems. Rote practice has its place as a tool; being able to perform it shouldn't be the goal in itself.",
            "spaceId": "d00460c203779d21d96fcfc6102d7a72"
          }
        ],
        "pageInfo": {
          "hasNextPage": false
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
